==Russian==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Ru-год.ogg|Audio|lang=ru}}
* {{ru-IPA|го́д}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|orv|ru}} {{term|годъ||time, period|lang=orv}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ru}} {{m|ine-pro|*gʰedʰ-||to unite, be associated, be suitable}}. Cognates include Ukrainian {{l|uk|годi}} (enough), Bulgarian {{l|bg|годе}} ([[ever]], as in {{l|bg|кой-годе}} = whoever), Czech {{l|cs|hod}}, Polish {{l|pl|gódy}} (feast), Upper Sorbian [[hody]] (Christmas), Lower Sorbian [[gódy]] (Christmas), Latvian {{l|lv|gads}} (year), German {{l|de|Gatte}} (husband) and {{l|de|gätlich}} (convenient), as well as English [[gather]] and [[good]], Dutch {{l|nl|goed}}, and German {{l|de|gut}}. Descendants include Russian {{l|ru|погода}}, {{l|ru|выгода}}, {{l|ru|угода}}, {{l|ru|годный}}, and {{l|ru|годиться}}.

===Noun===
{{ru-noun|год|m-in|го́да|го́ды|pl2=года́|pl3=лета́}}

# [[year]]
#: {{ux|ru|[[в]] [[этот|э́том]] '''году́'''|this year|inline=y}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[года́ми]]|for years; for years on end|inline=y}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[девяностый|девяно́стые]] '''го́ды'''|the '90s|inline=y}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[учебный|уче́бный]] '''год'''|school year; academic year|inline=y}}
#:* {{lang|ru|[[новый|Но́вый]] год}} — ''New Year’s Day''
#:* {{lang|ru|[[он|Ему́]] [[двадцать один|два́дцать оди́н]] год}} — ''He is 21 years old.''
#:* {{lang|ru|[[он|Ему́]] [[двадцать три|два́дцать три]] го́да}} — ''He is 23 years old.''
#:* {{lang|ru|[[он|Ему́]] [[двадцать пять|два́дцать пять]] [[лето|лет]]}} — ''He is 25 years old.''
#:* {{lang|ru|[[тысяча]] [[девятьсот]] [[девяносто]] [[второй]] год}} (týsjača devjatʹsót devjanósto vtorój god) {{g|m}} - (year) 1992 (''in words'')
#:* {{lang|ru|[[две]] [[тысяча|тысячи]] [[одиннадцатый]] год}} (dve týsjači odínnadcatyj god) {{g|m}} - (year) 2011 (''in words'')
#: {{ux|ru|[[с]] [[каждый|ка́ждым]] '''го́дом'''|from year to year, year by year, year after year|inline=y}}

====Usage notes====
* Use the appropriate case of '''''год''''' after simple or compound numbers ending in ''[[один]]'' (1), ''[[два]]'' (2), ''[[три]]'' (3), or ''[[четыре]]'' (4), except for 11, 12, 13 and 14 (and 111 - 114, 211 - 214 etc.) - for these and all other numbers, and with [[adverb]]s of quantity (''[[много]]'', ''[[сколько]]'', etc.), use the appropriate case of '''''[[лето]]'''.
